          },
          "committer": {
            "name": "Danny Weinberg",
            "email": "danny.weinberg@discordapp.com",
            "date": "2019-05-20T16:57:36Z"
          },
          "message": "Fix copts and linkopts relying on input files\n\nIn https://github.com/discordapp/rules_swift/commit/32275ca0536eca5610a915f7b26cb841ca0031a3 when the additional_input local variable was introduced, this went from passing `ctx.attr.swiftc_inputs` to passing `ctx.files.swiftc_inputs` into `expand_locations`. This breaks, since the underlying `expand_location` only allows `Target` types, resulting in the following error when passing any file-like target to `swiftc_inputs`:\n\n```\nexpected type 'Target' for 'targets' element but got type 'File' instead\n```\n\nThis switches the two `expand_locations` calls back to using `ctx.attr.swiftc_inputs`.",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "01c5d8503113ea349211f59fcb2395fd9d3bc02d",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/rules_swift/git/trees/01c5d8503113ea349211f59fcb2395fd9d3bc02d"
          },
